WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.633
- Are you a fan of reading?

00:00:01.633 --> 00:00:02.810
(man roaring)

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:03.643
Me neither.

00:00:03.643 --> 00:00:07.020
Luckily, now books come in
convenient talking picture form.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.060
And today, we'll pit two of the greatest

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:12.550
novel to movie franchises
ever against each other.

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:15.070
It's a battle for the
winningest wizarding world

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:16.990
in the world.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.150
As Harry Potter and his Hogwarts gang

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:22.160
take on the Middle-earth alumni
from "Lord of The Rings".

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:23.779
- Scared Potter?

00:00:23.779 --> 00:00:25.150
- You wish.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.100
- We're lining up the entire franchises

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.870
on the battlefield here and
that includes the prequels,

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.360
who I usually make sit at
the kids table, not today.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.150
Here's how we'll determine a winner.

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:37.040
Round one, Box Office.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:40.210
Round two, Tomatometer/audience score.

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:42.330
Round three, Characters,

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:44.950
and then I'll do a wildcard
round before I unleash

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:48.170
the verdict rendering to
all you muggles out there.

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:49.800
Spells will be cast,

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.450
names will be mispronounced,

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.750
and dwarfs will probably
run out of breath.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:55.583
- What about breakfast?

00:00:55.583 --> 00:00:57.320
- You've already had it.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:58.570
- We've had one, yes.

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:00.103
What about second breakfast?

00:01:01.318 --> 00:01:02.749
(soft music)

00:01:02.749 --> 00:01:04.530
(bell ringing)
- Round one, Box Office.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.760
I know seven magic rings aren't cheap

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:09.300
and I'm sure tuition at
Hogwarts might involve

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.480
some serious student loan debt.

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:13.610
But I'm pretty sure the
worldwide Box Office tally

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:16.660
of either of these franchises
could cover the bill.

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:18.710
You ready to hear about a ton of bread?

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:21.740
How about $12.2 billion.

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:23.630
That's the total worldwide haul

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:26.920
brought in by the 10 films in
the "Harry Potter" franchise.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:30.820
Eight movies plus the two
"Fantastic Beasts" movies.

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:33.000
Because "The Lord of The
Rings" films tapped out at six,

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.130
we're not expecting them
to compete with 12 bill.

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:40.770
But they still raked in $7.88
billion across the globe,

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:43.780
making for a better per
film average than Harry.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:46.410
If we just take the classic
"Lord of The Rings" trilogy,

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:48.760
versus the proper "Harry Potter" catalog,

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:51.480
as in, dude actually
shows up in the movies,

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.780
team "Hobbit" edges out team Gryffindor,

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.810
with the worldwide per film average

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:59.523
of $1.56 billion to $1.33 billion.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.131
I'd take either amount of money.

00:02:02.131 --> 00:02:05.381
(gentle chiming bells)

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.350
Those average numbers
intensify when we look

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:13.597
at the prequels each franchise spawned.

00:02:13.597 --> 00:02:16.320
"Fantastic Beasts", those
movies boast a world-wide

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.150
per film average of $550 million,

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:21.180
while the three "Hobbit"
flicks can brag about

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:24.410
averaging one billion dollars per movie.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.510
Yes, you heard it here first.

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:27.680
All six "Lord of The
Rings" films have grossed

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.120
at least one billion
dollars over the world

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.900
adjusted for inflation.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:33.830
So just imagine how much
money those flicks made

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:34.990
in Middle-earth.

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:36.980
Is that like a documentary for them?

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:39.970
Are Peter Jackson's movies
like, the last dance

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:41.550
of Middle-earth?
- No.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:43.767
- It's amazing how
popular and bank friendly

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:45.727
"The Lord of The Rings"
films have been since

00:02:45.727 --> 00:02:47.180
"The Fellowship of The
Rings" kicked us off

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:48.950
