00:10:53.123 --> 00:10:55.706
(bright music)

00:10:57.513 --> 00:10:59.360
- It's an accomplishment just getting us

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:02.120
into the theaters so many
times for one franchise.

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:03.970
And it's all the more
impressive that the final

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:06.610
climactic clash between good and evil,

00:11:06.610 --> 00:11:07.871
lived up to the hype.

00:11:07.871 --> 00:11:10.130
Even though I maintained Voldemort did not

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:11.500
have his A game that day,

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:13.900
you gotta give props to
Harry, Hermione and Ron

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:17.740
for coming together, one last
time, when it mattered most.

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:20.293
- Let's finish this the
way it started, together!

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:23.440
- With "Lord of The Rings",
I love thinking about

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:25.970
the contrast from one set to the next.

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:28.870
The Shire looks like such
a relaxing hippie village,

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:30.700
and I think that Woodstock
could've been annual

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:32.150
summer tradition there.

00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:35.160
Juxtapose that with the
volcanic intensity of Mordor,

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:37.770
and then remind yourself
that our brave little soul,

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:41.610
trying to take the ring there,
is from that late 60s Beatles

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:44.470
commune place, The Shire, crazy.

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:46.630
- One does not simply walk into Mordor.

00:11:46.630 --> 00:11:48.356
- There's also epic
battle scenes that rank up

00:11:48.356 --> 00:11:51.887
there as some of the best action
sequences ever put to film.

00:11:51.887 --> 00:11:54.070
"The Battle of the Five
Armies" is impressive

00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:55.150
in sheer scope.

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:58.210
But I'm talking about the
intimate hand-to-hand combat.

00:11:58.210 --> 00:12:02.420
Or in Legolas' case,
hand-to-arrow, to face combat.

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:04.460
I love that shot of him in the rain,

00:12:04.460 --> 00:12:05.880
sliding on the stairs,

00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:07.240
knocking down baddies like

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:09.420
he's Ray Allen draining corner threes.

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:11.142
Damn it, I went sports again.

00:12:11.142 --> 00:12:12.623
I'm so sorry y'all.

00:12:13.492 --> 00:12:14.325
- You're hopeless.

00:12:14.325 --> 00:12:15.990
- And then perhaps the
most surprising legacy

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:17.200
left by "Harry Potter",

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:20.280
Quidditch is an actual
sport played all over

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:21.950
the world, seriously.

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:25.030
It's replaced Frisbee golf as
the go-to college kids sport

00:12:25.030 --> 00:12:25.863
of our time.

00:12:25.863 --> 00:12:27.690
"Lord of The Rings" can't
match "Harry Potter"

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:30.350
in terms of intramural
athletic accomplishments,

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:31.580
so it'll have to be content

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:34.707
with it's incredible run at the Oscars.

00:12:34.707 --> 00:12:37.370
"Return of The King"
won every award category

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:38.850
in which it was nominated,

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:41.000
making it a perfect 11 for 11,

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:43.860
including best picture and best director.

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:46.840
Only two other films
ever, have won 11 Oscars.

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:48.410
Can you name them?

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:49.243
I'll wait.

00:12:49.243 --> 00:12:51.460
It's "Titanic" and "Ben-Hur."

00:12:51.460 --> 00:12:52.633
- Don't you let go.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.680
- So lots of folks think Andy Serkis

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:57.820
should've been recognized
for his work as Gollum,

00:12:57.820 --> 00:13:00.070
but he'll have to be
happy, with that character

00:13:00.070 --> 00:13:02.910
helping the movies take
a drastic leap forward

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:04.779
in terms of visual effects.

00:13:04.779 --> 00:13:08.110
Plus, everyone has tried a
Gollum impression at a party.

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:11.054
Usually doesn't go well,
no, I'm not going to try.

00:13:11.054 --> 00:13:11.887
- My

00:13:14.263 --> 00:13:15.096
precious!

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:17.930
(Gollum roaring)

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:21.340
- Both franchises had their
inaugural films released in 2001

00:13:21.340 --> 00:13:23.510
as Stanley Kubrick foretold.

00:13:23.510 --> 00:13:26.160
And while both have promising
futures with prequels,

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:28.770
Broadway shows, and streaming
seasons in the works,

00:13:28.770 --> 00:13:30.330
it is the opinion of this court,

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:31.597
that "The Lord of The Rings"
(bell ringing)

00:13:31.597 --> 00:13:35.660
is a hair more iconic, a thin, wispy hair,

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:38.506
like one of the ones
on Gollum's comb over.

00:13:38.506 --> 00:13:39.510
- Yes!

00:13:39.510 --> 00:13:41.210
- It is a precious win indeed,

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:44.550
because now we're tied
at two rounds a piece.

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:46.010
- A day may come

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:48.240
when the courage of men fails,

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:49.800
when we forsake our friends

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:52.130
and break all bonds of fellowship,

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:54.560
but it is not this day,

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:55.860
this day we fight!

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:58.380
- So once again, it's up to
me to step up to the plate

00:13:58.380 --> 00:14:01.425
and render a verdict that will
be scrutinized for all time.

00:14:01.425 --> 00:14:02.570
- What?

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:04.590
- And perhaps the bloodiest battle yet,

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:05.920
I'm giving this win

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:08.430
to "Lord of The Rings".
(bell ringing)

00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:09.280
- It's done.

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:11.830
- Maybe its because the
source material came out first

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:14.860
or I saw all these movies
multiple times in theaters,

00:14:14.860 --> 00:14:17.120
but it's no shame to "Harry Potter."

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:19.390
Harry doesn't care about
me, he's in New York,

00:14:19.390 --> 00:14:21.670
and he's got that cursed
child to worry about.

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:23.420
That show is always sold out.

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:24.530
- Ready?

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:25.363
- Ready.

00:14:28.370 --> 00:14:30.110
- All any of us care about is what you

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:31.580
the viewer has to say.

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:33.860
So comment below and type in your vote.

00:14:33.860 --> 00:14:36.830
Are you going L-O-T-R or H-P?

00:14:36.830 --> 00:14:39.140
Together those letters spell PHLORT.

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:41.420
So as long as your answer
makes more sense than that,

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:42.740
we're good.

00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:45.140
- This is completely mental.
- Completely.

00:14:45.140 --> 00:14:46.880
- Keep it classy out
there on the inter-web,

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:48.400
I'd love to stay and chat more,

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:50.713
but I booked an eagle to whisk me home.

00:14:51.650 --> 00:14:53.150
It'll be here now, any second.

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:55.810
They're never on time.

00:14:55.810 --> 00:14:57.470
Oh wait, I'm already home.

00:14:57.470 --> 00:14:58.759
Cancel the eagle.

00:14:58.759 --> 00:15:01.342
(upbeat music)

